<div data-section-type="content-tabs" class="content-tabs tcc-section-padding">
  <div class="content-tabs__inner tcc-page-width">
    {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="content-tabs__eyebrow tcc-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="content-tabs__heading tcc-heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="content-tabs__buttons" role="tablist">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            class="content-tabs__button{% if forloop.first %} content-tabs__button--active{% endif %}"
            aria-selected="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
            aria-controls="content-tab-panel-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index0 }}"
            data-tab-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
            {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
          >
            {{ block.settings.label }}
          </button>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        <div
          id="content-tab-panel-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index0 }}"
          class="content-tabs__panel{% if forloop.first %} content-tabs__panel--active{% endif %}"
          role="tabpanel"
          data-tab-panel="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
          {% unless forloop.first %}hidden{% endunless %}
        >
          <div class="content-tabs__card">
            <div class="content-tabs__card-text">
              {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
                <h3 class="content-tabs__card-title tcc-heading">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
                <p class="content-tabs__card-body tcc-body">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.checklist != blank -%}
                <ul class="content-tabs__checklist">
                  {%- assign checklist_items = block.settings.checklist | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
                  {%- for item in checklist_items -%}
                    {%- assign trimmed_item = item | strip -%}
                    {%- if trimmed_item != blank -%}
                      <li class="content-tabs__checklist-item tcc-body">
                        <span class="material-symbols-outlined content-tabs__check-icon">check</span>
                        <span>{{ trimmed_item }}</span>
                      </li>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            {%- if block.settings.image != blank or block.settings.external_image_url != blank -%}
              <div class="content-tabs__card-image">
                {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
                  <img src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 600 }}" alt="{{ block.settings.image.alt | escape | default: block.settings.title }}" width="{{ block.settings.image.width }}" height="{{ block.settings.image.height }}" loading="lazy">
                {%- elsif block.settings.external_image_url != blank -%}
                  <img src="{{ block.settings.external_image_url }}" alt="{{ block.settings.title | escape }}" width="600" height="600" loading="lazy">
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .content-tabs {
    background: var(--tcc-bg);
  }
  .content-tabs__eyebrow {
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .content-tabs__heading {
    font-size: var(--tcc-fs-h2);
    font-weight: var(--tcc-fw-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tcc-ls-display);
    line-height: var(--tcc-lh-tight);
    color: var(--tcc-ink);
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem 0;
  }

  .content-tabs__buttons {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .content-tabs__button {
    font-family: var(--tcc-font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: var(--tcc-fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1;
    border-radius: var(--tcc-radius);
    padding: 14px 20px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--tcc-ink-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--tcc-line);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .content-tabs__button--active {
    background: var(--tcc-ink);
    color: var(--tcc-bg);
    border-color: var(--tcc-ink);
  }
  .content-tabs__button:hover:not(.content-tabs__button--active) {
    background: var(--tcc-line);
    color: var(--tcc-ink);
  }

  .content-tabs__panel { display: none; }
  .content-tabs__panel--active { display: block; }
  .content-tabs__panel[hidden] { display: none; }

  .content-tabs__card {
    background: var(--tcc-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--tcc-line);
    border-radius: var(--tcc-radius);
    padding: 2.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .content-tabs__card:has(.content-tabs__card-image) {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
  }

  .content-tabs__card-title {
    font-size: 24px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-weight: var(--tcc-fw-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    color: var(--tcc-ink);
  }
  .content-tabs__card-body {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: var(--tcc-lh-body);
    color: var(--tcc-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .content-tabs__checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .content-tabs__checklist-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--tcc-ink);
  }
  .content-tabs__check-icon {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--tcc-positive);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-variation-settings: 'FILL' 0, 'wght' 700;
  }

  .content-tabs__card-image {
    max-width: 320px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .content-tabs__card-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--tcc-radius);
    display: block;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .content-tabs__heading { font-size: 24px; }
    .content-tabs__button { font-size: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; }
    .content-tabs__card { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; padding: 1.5rem; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .content-tabs__card-image { max-width: 100%; order: -1; }
    .content-tabs__card-title { font-size: 19px; }
    .content-tabs__card-body { font-size: 14px; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  (function () {
    var section = document.querySelector('[data-section-type="content-tabs"]');
    if (!section) return;
    var buttons = section.querySelectorAll('.content-tabs__button');
    var panels = section.querySelectorAll('.content-tabs__panel');
    buttons.forEach(function (button) {
      button.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var index = this.getAttribute('data-tab-index');
        buttons.forEach(function (btn) {
          btn.classList.remove('content-tabs__button--active');
          btn.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'false');
        });
        panels.forEach(function (panel) {
          panel.classList.remove('content-tabs__panel--active');
          panel.setAttribute('hidden', '');
        });
        this.classList.add('content-tabs__button--active');
        this.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'true');
        var activePanel = section.querySelector('[data-tab-panel="' + index + '"]');
        if (activePanel) {
          activePanel.classList.add('content-tabs__panel--active');
          activePanel.removeAttribute('hidden');
        }
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Content Tabs",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "The Details" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Two reading paths — pick yours." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "tab",
      "name": "Tab",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Tab label", "default": "Tab" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Content title", "default": "Tab title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Content body" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "checklist", "label": "Checklist items", "info": "One item per line" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "external_image_url", "label": "External Image URL" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Content Tabs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Cardiovascular & circulatory health",
            "title": "What the cardiovascular research shows.",
            "body": "Chen et al. (2022, Frontiers in Cardiovascular Medicine) followed 1,062 adults for 12 months on 10,800 FU/day of nattokinase. Carotid plaque area decreased by up to 36%; arterial wall thickness decreased by ~22%; LDL fell 18% and HDL rose 16%; 0 adverse events. Authors conclude the clinically active range is 6,000–12,000 FU per day.",
            "checklist": "1,062 adults studied for 12 months\n36% carotid plaque-area reduction (at 10,800 FU/day)\n22% arterial wall thickness reduction\n18% LDL drop, 16% HDL rise\n0 adverse events at the studied dose"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Recent research on post-viral microvascular health",
            "title": "Recent research on post-viral microvascular health.",
            "body": "Two newer findings widen nattokinase's relevance. Tanikawa et al. (2022, Molecules) showed in vitro that purified nattokinase degrades the SARS-CoV-2 spike protein and ACE2 in 60–180 minutes — a cell-lysate / lab-bench study, not yet a human trial. Grixti, Pretorius & Kell (2024, preprint) showed recombinant nattokinase degrades fibrinaloid microclots — anomalous, fibrinolysis-resistant clots documented in Long COVID and ME/CFS — within 2 hours in vitro. Both are mechanistic; neither is a human RCT yet.",
            "checklist": "Tanikawa 2022 (Molecules): in vitro spike-protein degradation in 60–180 min\nGrixti / Kell 2024 (preprint): fibrinaloid microclot degradation in vitro\nBoth are mechanism-of-action studies — not yet human RCTs"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "label": "How to take",
            "title": "Dose to your protocol.",
            "body": "Take 1–3 capsules per day with water, ideally on an empty stomach (30 minutes before food works best). 1 capsule = 4,000 FU; 3 capsules = ~12,000 FU, within the 6,000–12,000 FU clinically active range. Many users start at 1 capsule and titrate up over a few weeks with their clinician's input.",
            "checklist": "1 capsule daily = 4,000 FU (entry-level)\n2 capsules daily = ~8,000 FU (within clinical range)\n3 capsules daily = ~12,000 FU (matches Chen 2022 range)\nEmpty stomach for best absorption"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Safety & interactions",
            "title": "Designed for blood-thinner-aware users.",
            "body": "Vitamin K2 can interact with vitamin-K-antagonist anticoagulants like warfarin. We removed it for compatibility, and offer K2 separately. If you take warfarin, DOACs (Eliquis, Xarelto, Pradaxa), aspirin, or any blood-thinning medication — or are pregnant, nursing, or have a bleeding disorder — consult your healthcare provider before use.",
            "checklist": "K2-free formulation — vitamin-K-antagonist friendly\nThird-party tested for heavy metals\nManufactured in FDA-registered facility\nGMP certified, every batch"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
